{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 210,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This has nothing to do with physics, but - Racewalking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3240,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here are the rules: Walk so that one foot\nis always on the ground and keep your front"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7100,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leg straight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8100,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In short, do a funny walk, really fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10280,
    "dDurationMs": 3649,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's also something funny about the rules,\nthough - the judges who determine whether"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13929,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or not a competitor is indeed \"walking\", are\nonly allowed to stand stationary at the side"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17539,
    "dDurationMs": 4181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the course and judge by EYE whether the\ncompetitors APPEAR to be walking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21720,
    "dDurationMs": 3769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You'd think that for a sport whose definition\nis so technical, they'd appeal to all possible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25489,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "technology to enforce the rules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27619,
    "dDurationMs": 1940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So is race walking stuck in the dark ages?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29559,
    "dDurationMs": 4031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, there are other sports that don't\nallow referees to view replays, but when you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33590,
    "dDurationMs": 3739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "think about the electronics of fencing, the\nfinish-line cameras of track and field, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37329,
    "dDurationMs": 4271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "touchpads of swimming, and the 3D ball tracking\nand path-reconstruction of tennis… race"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41600,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "walking judges, on the other hand, seem quite\npedestrian."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44280,
    "dDurationMs": 4869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're even forbidden to watch from ground\nlevel or use such modern technology as binoculars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49149,
    "dDurationMs": 1021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or a mirror."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50170,
    "dDurationMs": 2950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what's up with all this perambulatory red\ntape?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53120,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you look carefully at slowmo footage or\nbasically any photograph of racewalkers themselves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57730,
    "dDurationMs": 3009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'll realize that pretty much everyone leaves\nthe ground…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60739,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not just occasionally because of a push or\nstumble, which is allowed - but on almost"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64439,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every stride."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65439,
    "dDurationMs": 4521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, it is WELL RECOGNIZED by the racewalking\ncommunity that most racewalkers regularly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69960,
    "dDurationMs": 4769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leave the ground and may even be in the air\nup to 10% of the time… so EVERYONE is breaking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74729,
    "dDurationMs": 1051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the rules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75780,
    "dDurationMs": 4310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, there are plenty of arbitrary rules in\nsport… but the fact that most athletes break"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80090,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the traditional DEFINING rule for this sport,\nis, to say the least…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84170,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "surprising."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85170,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this isn't like the suspicion that almost\nall professional cyclists are doping, because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89020,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unlike our constant struggle to test and catch\ndopers, we are well within the technological"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93230,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "means to catch \"ungrounded\" racewalkers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95770,
    "dDurationMs": 4349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It seems clear that the technophobia in racewalking\nstems from the fact that if racewalkers started"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100119,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "using high speed cameras, they might no longer\nhave a sport."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103579,
    "dDurationMs": 3941,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that brings into question the very essence\nof sport - because all games, really, are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107520,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just an arbitrary set of rules and limitations\nthat we submit to for the purpose of having"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111130,
    "dDurationMs": 1279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fun and challenging ourselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112409,
    "dDurationMs": 5391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, there's a reason that track and field\nforbids bicycles, cycling forbids motorcycles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117800,
    "dDurationMs": 2419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and motorcycle racing forbids rockets…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120219,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe those reasons are just as arbitrary\nas racewalking's ban on technology… because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124509,
    "dDurationMs": 4101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the goal isn't to keep your feet on the ground\n- it's to see who's fastest doing a funny"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128610,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "walk, just like triple jump is to see who\ncan go the farthest doing a funny jump, hurdles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132660,
    "dDurationMs": 3830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are to see who can run the fastest with plastic\nbarriers in the way, and tennis is to see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136490,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who can hit a ball over a net the best, but\nonly within certain carefully drawn lines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140300,
    "dDurationMs": 3070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and with a racquet and not a paddle or hands\nor feet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143370,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sport, ultimately, is not about the sport,\nbut about the players and their struggles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148970,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's about how far we're able to push the\nboundaries of human ability… within the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152060,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "boundaries set by the rules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153980,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So is racewalking a sport in denial, desperately\nholding on to its past and blatantly refusing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158170,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to accept technological advances that in principle\nimprove the judging of the sport, but in reality"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162340,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shake its very foundations?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163540,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't know… but are racewalkers athletes?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167420,
    "dDurationMs": 15810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most certainly."
    } ]
  } ]
}
